(   [Problem Statement]: State Rolle's Theorem, give its geometrical interpretation, and provide a rigorous proof based on the Extreme Value Theorem.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formal Statement of Rolle's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Let f: [a, b] -> R be a function satisfying three conditions:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) f\(x\) is continuous on the closed interval [a, b].) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) f\(x\) is differentiable on the open interval \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) f\(a\) = f\(b\).) Tj
T*
(   Then there exists at least one point c in the open interval \(a, b\) such that f'\(c\) = 0.) Tj
T*
ET

