(   2. Geometrical Interpretation:) Tj
T*
(   - The graph of y = f\(x\) connects points A\(a, f\(a\)\) and B\(b, f\(b\)\) where both endpoints have) Tj
T*
(   identical heights \(f\(a\) = f\(b\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - The theorem asserts that if the curve is smooth \(no sharp corners\) and unbroken, there must) Tj
T*
(   be at least one point \(c, f\(c\)\) between A and B where the tangent line is horizontal \(parallel) Tj
T*
(   to the x-axis\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Rigorous Analytical Proof:) Tj
T*
(   - Since f\(x\) is continuous on the closed bounded interval [a, b], by the Weierstrass Extreme) Tj
T*
(   Value Theorem, f attains its global maximum M and global minimum m on [a, b]:) Tj
T*
(   M = max_{x in [a, b]} f\(x\), m = min_{x in [a, b]} f\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case 1: M = m.) Tj
T*
(   Then f\(x\) is a constant function: f\(x\) = M for all x in [a, b].) Tj
T*
(   The derivative of a constant function is zero everywhere: f'\(x\) = 0 for all x in \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   Thus any point c in \(a, b\) satisfies f'\(c\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Case 2: M != m.) Tj
T*
(   Since f\(a\) = f\(b\), at least one of M or m must be attained at an interior point c in \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   Without loss of generality, assume the maximum M is attained at c in \(a, b\), so f\(c\) >= f\(x\)) Tj
T*
(   for all x in [a, b].) Tj
T*
(   Since f is differentiable on \(a, b\), f'\(c\) exists and equals both one-sided limits:) Tj
T*
(   * Left-hand derivative: For h < 0 \(sufficiently small\):) Tj
T*
(   f\(c + h\) - f\(c\) <= 0 => [f\(c + h\) - f\(c\)] / h >= 0 \(since h < 0\).) Tj
T*
(   Taking limit h -> 0-: f'\(c\) >= 0.) Tj
T*
(   * Right-hand derivative: For h > 0 \(sufficiently small\):) Tj
T*
(   f\(c + h\) - f\(c\) <= 0 => [f\(c + h\) - f\(c\)] / h <= 0 \(since h > 0\).) Tj
T*
(   Taking limit h -> 0+: f'\(c\) <= 0.) Tj
T*
(   Since f'\(c\) exists:) Tj
T*
(   0 <= f'\(c\) <= 0 => f'\(c\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, there exists c in \(a, b\) such that f'\(c\) = 0. \(Hence proved\).) Tj
T*
