BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove Lagrange's Mean Value Theorem \(LMVT\). Use it to prove that for all x > 0: x / \(1 + x\) < ln\(1 + x\) < x.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of LMVT:) Tj
T*
(   If a real function f\(x\) is continuous on [a, b] and differentiable on \(a, b\), then there exists) Tj
T*
(   at least one point c in \(a, b\) such that:) Tj
T*
(   f'\(c\) = [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ] / \(b - a\),) Tj
T*
(   or equivalently: f\(b\) = f\(a\) + \(b - a\) * f'\(c\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Proof using Auxiliary Function:) Tj
T*
(   - Construct the function phi\(x\) = f\(x\) - k * x, where constant k is chosen such that phi\(a\) =) Tj
T*
(   phi\(b\):) Tj
T*
(   f\(a\) - k * a = f\(b\) - k * b => k * \(b - a\) = f\(b\) - f\(a\) => k = [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ] / \(b - a\).) Tj
T*
(   - Verify conditions of Rolle's theorem for phi\(x\) on [a, b]:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) phi\(x\) is continuous on [a, b] \(sum of continuous functions\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) phi\(x\) is differentiable on \(a, b\) \(sum of differentiable functions\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) phi\(a\) = phi\(b\) by construction.) Tj
T*
(   - By Rolle's Theorem, there exists c in \(a, b\) such that phi'\(c\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   phi'\(c\) = f'\(c\) - k = 0 => f'\(c\) = k = [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ] / \(b - a\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Application: Proving x / \(1 + x\) < ln\(1 + x\) < x for x > 0:) Tj
T*
(   - Consider f\(t\) = ln\(1 + t\) on the interval [0, x] where x > 0.) Tj
T*
(   - f\(t\) is continuous on [0, x] and differentiable on \(0, x\) with f'\(t\) = 1 / \(1 + t\).) Tj
T*
(   - By LMVT: [ f\(x\) - f\(0\) ] / \(x - 0\) = f'\(c\) for some c in \(0, x\):) Tj
T*
(   [ ln\(1 + x\) - ln\(1\) ] / x = 1 / \(1 + c\)) Tj
T*
ET

