(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: State and prove Cauchy's Mean Value Theorem \(CMVT\). Deduce Lagrange's Mean Value Theorem as a particular case.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Statement of Cauchy's Mean Value Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Let f\(x\) and g\(x\) be two functions such that:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) f\(x\) and g\(x\) are continuous on the closed interval [a, b].) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) f\(x\) and g\(x\) are differentiable on the open interval \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) g'\(x\) != 0 for all x in \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   Then there exists at least one point c in \(a, b\) such that:) Tj
T*
(   [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ] / [ g\(b\) - g\(a\) ] = f'\(c\) / g'\(c\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Proof of CMVT:) Tj
T*
(   - First, note that g\(b\) - g\(a\) != 0.) Tj
T*
(   If g\(b\) = g\(a\), by Rolle's Theorem there would exist xi in \(a, b\) with g'\(xi\) = 0,) Tj
T*
(   contradicting condition \(c\).) Tj
T*
(   - Define an auxiliary function F\(x\) on [a, b]:) Tj
T*
(   F\(x\) = f\(x\) - A * g\(x\),) Tj
T*
(   where constant A is chosen such that F\(a\) = F\(b\):) Tj
T*
(   f\(a\) - A * g\(a\) = f\(b\) - A * g\(b\)) Tj
T*
(   => A * [ g\(b\) - g\(a\) ] = f\(b\) - f\(a\)) Tj
T*
(   => A = [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ] / [ g\(b\) - g\(a\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - F\(x\) satisfies Rolle's theorem on [a, b]:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) F\(x\) is continuous on [a, b].) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) F\(x\) is differentiable on \(a, b\).) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) F\(a\) = F\(b\).) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, there exists c in \(a, b\) such that F'\(c\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   F'\(c\) = f'\(c\) - A * g'\(c\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   => A * g'\(c\) = f'\(c\)) Tj
T*
(   => A = f'\(c\) / g'\(c\) \(since g'\(c\) != 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Equating the two expressions for A:) Tj
T*
(   [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ] / [ g\(b\) - g\(a\) ] = f'\(c\) / g'\(c\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Deduction of Lagrange's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   - Set g\(x\) = x.) Tj
T*
(   - Then g'\(x\) = 1 != 0 everywhere, and g\(b\) - g\(a\) = b - a.) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting into CMVT:) Tj
T*
(   [ f\(b\) - f\(a\) ] / \(b - a\) = f'\(c\) / 1 = f'\(c\).) Tj
T*
(   - This is precisely Lagrange's Mean Value Theorem.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
