(   1. Statement of Taylor's Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   Let f: [a, a + h] -> R be such that f, f', f'', ..., f^\(n-1\) are continuous on [a, a + h] and) Tj
T*
(   f^\(n\) exists on \(a, a + h\).) Tj
T*
(   Then:) Tj
T*
(   f\(a + h\) = f\(a\) + h * f'\(a\) + \(h^2 / 2!\) * f''\(a\) + ... + [ h^\(n-1\) / \(n - 1\)! ] * f^\(n-1\)\(a\) +) Tj
T*
(   R_n,) Tj
T*
(   where R_n is the Remainder term after n terms.) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation using Auxiliary Function:) Tj
T*
(   - For x in [a, a + h], define:) Tj
T*
(   phi\(x\) = f\(a + h\) - [ f\(x\) + \(a + h - x\)*f'\(x\) + \(\(a + h - x\)^2 / 2!\)*f''\(x\) + ... + \(\(a + h -) Tj
T*
(   x\)^\(n-1\) / \(n-1\)!\)*f^\(n-1\)\(x\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Note that at x = a + h, all terms vanish except f\(a + h\) - f\(a + h\) = 0, so phi\(a + h\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - At x = a, phi\(a\) = R_n.) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiate phi\(x\) with respect to x \(terms telescope pairwise\):) Tj
T*
(   phi'\(x\) = -f'\(x\) - [ -f'\(x\) + \(a+h-x\)*f''\(x\) ] - [ -\(a+h-x\)*f''\(x\) + \(\(a+h-x\)^2/2!\)*f'''\(x\) ] -) Tj
T*
(   ...) Tj
T*
(   = - [ \(a + h - x\)^\(n-1\) / \(n - 1\)! ] * f^\(n\)\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Now choose another function psi\(x\) = \(a + h - x\)^p, where p >= 1 is an integer.) Tj
T*
(   Then psi\(a + h\) = 0, psi\(a\) = h^p, and psi'\(x\) = -p * \(a + h - x\)^\(p - 1\).) Tj
T*
(   - Apply Cauchy's Mean Value Theorem to phi\(x\) and psi\(x\) on [a, a + h]:) Tj
T*
(   [ phi\(a + h\) - phi\(a\) ] / [ psi\(a + h\) - psi\(a\) ] = phi'\(c\) / psi'\(c\) for some c in \(a, a + h\).) Tj
T*
(   [ 0 - R_n ] / [ 0 - h^p ] = R_n / h^p = [ - \(\(a + h - c\)^\(n-1\) / \(n - 1\)!\) * f^\(n\)\(c\) ] / [ -p) Tj
T*
(   * \(a + h - c\)^\(p - 1\) ]) Tj
T*
(   => R_n = [ h^p / \(p * \(n - 1\)!\) ] * \(a + h - c\)^\(n - p\) * f^\(n\)\(c\).) Tj
T*
(   - Write c = a + theta * h, where 0 < theta < 1. Then a + h - c = h * \(1 - theta\).) Tj
T*
(   General Schlomilch-Roche Remainder:) Tj
T*
(   R_n = [ h^n * \(1 - theta\)^\(n - p\) / \(p * \(n - 1\)!\) ] * f^\(n\)\(a + theta * h\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Deduction of Specific Remainder Forms:) Tj
T*
(   - Lagrange's Form of Remainder \(set p = n\):) Tj
T*
(   R_n = [ h^n / n! ] * f^\(n\)\(a + theta * h\), where 0 < theta < 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Cauchy's Form of Remainder \(set p = 1\):) Tj
T*
(   R_n = [ h^n * \(1 - theta\)^\(n - 1\) / \(n - 1\)! ] * f^\(n\)\(a + theta * h\), where 0 < theta < 1.) Tj
T*
