(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Expand ln\(1 + x\) and e^x in Maclaurin series with remainder, state their intervals of convergence, and estimate the error when approximating e by its first 5 terms.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Maclaurin Series for e^x:) Tj
T*
(   - f\(x\) = e^x => f^\(n\)\(x\) = e^x for all n >= 0.) Tj
T*
(   - f^\(n\)\(0\) = 1 for all n.) Tj
T*
(   - Maclaurin expansion:) Tj
T*
(   e^x = 1 + x + x^2/2! + x^3/3! + ... + x^n/n! + R_n\(x\),) Tj
T*
(   where Lagrange remainder R_n\(x\) = [ x^n / n! ] * e^\(theta * x\), with 0 < theta < 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Since lim_{n -> infinity} x^n / n! = 0 for any real x, the series converges for all x in) Tj
T*
(   \(-infinity, infinity\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Error Estimation for e = e^1 using first 5 terms \(n = 5\):) Tj
T*
(   - Approximating polynomial: P_4\(1\) = 1 + 1 + 1/2! + 1/3! + 1/4! = 1 + 1 + 0.5 + 0.16667 +) Tj
T*
(   0.04167 = 2.70833.) Tj
T*
(   - Remainder R_5\(1\) = [ 1^5 / 5! ] * e^theta = \(1 / 120\) * e^theta, where 0 < theta < 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Since e^theta < e^1 < 3:) Tj
T*
(   Error |R_5\(1\)| < 3 / 120 = 0.025.) Tj
T*
(   - Exact e = 2.71828; actual error is |2.71828 - 2.70833| = 0.00995 < 0.025.) Tj
T*
(   3. Maclaurin Series for ln\(1 + x\):) Tj
T*
