(>> Solution to Question 10:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Prove L'Hopital's Rule for the indeterminate form 0/0 using Cauchy's Mean Value Theorem. Evaluate: lim_{x -> 0} [ \(e^x - e^\(-x\) - 2x\) / \(x - sin x\) ].) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Proof of L'Hopital's Rule \(0/0 form\):) Tj
T*
(   - Let f and g be functions differentiable on an open interval containing a \(except possibly at) Tj
T*
(   a\), such that:) Tj
T*
(   lim_{x -> a} f\(x\) = 0 and lim_{x -> a} g\(x\) = 0, with g'\(x\) != 0 for x != a.) Tj
T*
(   - Extend f and g to be continuous at x = a by defining f\(a\) = 0 and g\(a\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - For any x > a \(the case x < a is symmetric\), f and g are continuous on [a, x] and) Tj
T*
(   differentiable on \(a, x\).) Tj
T*
(   - By Cauchy's Mean Value Theorem, there exists c in \(a, x\) such that:) Tj
T*
(   [ f\(x\) - f\(a\) ] / [ g\(x\) - g\(a\) ] = f'\(c\) / g'\(c\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since f\(a\) = 0 and g\(a\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x\) / g\(x\) = f'\(c\) / g'\(c\).) Tj
T*
(   - As x -> a+, since a < c < x, the squeeze theorem forces c -> a+.) Tj
T*
(   - If lim_{t -> a} f'\(t\) / g'\(t\) = L exists, then:) Tj
T*
(   lim_{x -> a} f\(x\) / g\(x\) = lim_{c -> a} f'\(c\) / g'\(c\) = L. \(Hence proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Evaluation of lim_{x -> 0} [ \(e^x - e^\(-x\) - 2x\) / \(x - sin x\) ]:) Tj
T*
(   - At x = 0: Numerator = 1 - 1 - 0 = 0. Denominator = 0 - 0 = 0. \(Form 0/0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Apply L'Hopital's Rule \(Differentiate numerator and denominator\):) Tj
T*
(   L = lim_{x -> 0} [ \(e^x + e^\(-x\) - 2\) / \(1 - cos x\) ].) Tj
T*
(   At x = 0: Num = 1 + 1 - 2 = 0; Den = 1 - 1 = 0. \(Form 0/0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Apply L'Hopital's Rule second time:) Tj
T*
(   L = lim_{x -> 0} [ \(e^x - e^\(-x\)\) / \(sin x\) ].) Tj
T*
(   At x = 0: Num = 1 - 1 = 0; Den = 0. \(Form 0/0\).) Tj
T*
(   - Apply L'Hopital's Rule third time:) Tj
T*
(   L = lim_{x -> 0} [ \(e^x + e^\(-x\)\) / \(cos x\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Now substitute x = 0:) Tj
T*
(   Num = e^0 + e^0 = 1 + 1 = 2.) Tj
T*
(   Den = cos\(0\) = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Final Limit:) Tj
T*
(   L = 2 / 1 = 2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
