(   - Method 1: Using Maclaurin series of tan x:) Tj
T*
(   tan x = x + x^3/3 + 2x^5/15 + O\(x^7\).) Tj
T*
(   tan x - x = x^3/3 + 2x^5/15 + ...) Tj
T*
(   Therefore:) Tj
T*
(   L1 = lim_{x -> 0} [ \(x^3/3 + 2x^5/15 + ...\) / x^3 ] = lim_{x -> 0} [ 1/3 + 2x^2/15 + ... ] =) Tj
T*
(   1/3.) Tj
T*
(   - Method 2: By L'Hopital's Rule:) Tj
T*
(   L1 = lim_{x -> 0} [ \(sec^2 x - 1\) / \(3x^2\) ] = lim_{x -> 0} [ tan^2 x / \(3x^2\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = \(1/3\) * [ lim_{x -> 0} \(tan x / x\) ]^2 = \(1/3\) * \(1\)^2 = 1/3.) Tj
T*
(   2. Part \(ii\): Evaluate L2 = lim_{x -> 0} [ \(1 / x^2\) - \(1 / sin^2 x\) ] \(Form infinity -) Tj
T*
(   infinity\):) Tj
T*
(   - Combine into a single fraction:) Tj
T*
(   L2 = lim_{x -> 0} [ \(sin^2 x - x^2\) / \(x^2 * sin^2 x\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Factor the numerator as a difference of squares:) Tj
T*
(   sin^2 x - x^2 = \(sin x - x\) * \(sin x + x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Replace sin^2 x in denominator with x^2 using standard limit lim_{x -> 0} \(sin x / x\) = 1:) Tj
T*
(   x^2 * sin^2 x = x^4 * \(sin x / x\)^2 ~ x^4.) Tj
T*
(   - Rewrite limit:) Tj
T*
(   L2 = lim_{x -> 0} [ \(sin x - x\) / x^3 ] * [ \(sin x + x\) / x ].) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluate each factor:) Tj
T*
(   Factor 1: lim_{x -> 0} \(sin x - x\) / x^3:) Tj
T*
(   sin x = x - x^3/6 + x^5/120 - ... => \(sin x - x\)/x^3 = -1/6 + x^2/120 - ...) Tj
T*
(   lim = -1/6.) Tj
T*
(   Factor 2: lim_{x -> 0} \(sin x + x\) / x = lim \(sin x / x + 1\) = 1 + 1 = 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply the two limits:) Tj
T*
(   L2 = \(-1/6\) * 2 = -2/6 = -1/3.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   \(i\) Limit = 1/3.) Tj
T*
(   \(ii\) Limit = -1/3.) Tj
T*
