(>> Solution to Question 13:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Define curvature kappa and radius of curvature rho. Starting from the intrinsic definition kappa = dpsi / ds, rigorously derive the Cartesian formula: rho = [ 1 + \(y'\)^2 ]^\(3/2\) / |y''|.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definitions:) Tj
T*
(   - Let C be a smooth plane curve y = f\(x\). Let P be a point on C with arc length s measured from) Tj
T*
(   a fixed reference point.) Tj
T*
(   - Let psi be the angle that the tangent line at P makes with the positive x-axis.) Tj
T*
(   - The Curvature kappa is defined as the instantaneous rate of change of tangent inclination) Tj
T*
(   angle psi with respect to arc length s:) Tj
T*
(   kappa = dpsi / ds.) Tj
T*
(   - The Radius of Curvature rho is defined as the reciprocal of curvature:) Tj
T*
(   rho = 1 / |kappa| = |ds / dpsi|.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Derivation of Cartesian Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Relation between tangent slope and psi:) Tj
T*
(   Slope y' = dy / dx = tan\(psi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Differentiate both sides with respect to x:) Tj
T*
(   y'' = d^2 y / dx^2 = d/dx [ tan\(psi\) ] = sec^2\(psi\) * \(dpsi / dx\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: By the chain rule, relate dpsi/dx to arc length s:) Tj
T*
(   dpsi / dx = \(dpsi / ds\) * \(ds / dx\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute this into Step 2:) Tj
T*
(   y'' = sec^2\(psi\) * \(dpsi / ds\) * \(ds / dx\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Arc length differential:) Tj
T*
(   \(ds\)^2 = \(dx\)^2 + \(dy\)^2 => ds / dx = sqrt\(1 + \(dy/dx\)^2\) = sqrt\(1 + \(y'\)^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Express sec^2\(psi\) in terms of y':) Tj
T*
(   sec^2\(psi\) = 1 + tan^2\(psi\) = 1 + \(y'\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Substitute sec^2\(psi\) and ds/dx into the equation for y'':) Tj
T*
(   y'' = [ 1 + \(y'\)^2 ] * \(dpsi / ds\) * sqrt\(1 + \(y'\)^2\)) Tj
T*
(   = [ 1 + \(y'\)^2 ]^\(3/2\) * \(dpsi / ds\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 7: Solve for dpsi / ds = kappa:) Tj
T*
(   kappa = dpsi / ds = y'' / [ 1 + \(y'\)^2 ]^\(3/2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 8: Compute radius of curvature rho = |1 / kappa|:) Tj
T*
(   rho = [ 1 + \(y'\)^2 ]^\(3/2\) / |y''|. \(Hence proved\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
