(   1. Derivation of Parametric Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Let x = x\(t\), y = y\(t\). Denote derivatives with respect to t by dots or primes:) Tj
T*
(   y1 = dy / dx = \(dy/dt\) / \(dx/dt\) = y' / x'.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute second derivative y2 = d^2 y / dx^2:) Tj
T*
(   y2 = d/dx [ y' / x' ] = \(d/dt [ y' / x' ]\) / \(dx / dt\)) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(x' * y'' - y' * x''\) / \(x'\)^2 ] / x') Tj
T*
(   = \(x' * y'' - y' * x''\) / \(x'\)^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute y1 and y2 into the Cartesian curvature formula rho = [ 1 + y1^2 ]^\(3/2\) / |y2|:) Tj
T*
(   1 + y1^2 = 1 + \(y'/x'\)^2 = [ \(x'\)^2 + \(y'\)^2 ] / \(x'\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   [ 1 + y1^2 ]^\(3/2\) = [ \(x'\)^2 + \(y'\)^2 ]^\(3/2\) / \(x'\)^3.) Tj
T*
(   - Divide by |y2|:) Tj
T*
(   rho = [ [ \(x'\)^2 + \(y'\)^2 ]^\(3/2\) / \(x'\)^3 ] / [ |x' * y'' - y' * x''| / \(x'\)^3 ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ \(x'\)^2 + \(y'\)^2 ]^\(3/2\) / |x' * y'' - y' * x''|. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Radius of Curvature of the Cycloid:) Tj
T*
(   x = a*\(theta - sin theta\), y = a*\(1 - cos theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - First derivatives with respect to theta:) Tj
T*
(   x' = a*\(1 - cos theta\) = 2a * sin^2\(theta / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   y' = a * sin\(theta\) = 2a * sin\(theta / 2\) * cos\(theta / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Second derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   x'' = a * sin\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   y'' = a * cos\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Compute \(x'\)^2 + \(y'\)^2:) Tj
T*
(   \(x'\)^2 + \(y'\)^2 = a^2 * [ \(1 - cos theta\)^2 + sin^2\(theta\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * [ 1 - 2*cos theta + cos^2 theta + sin^2 theta ]) Tj
T*
(   = a^2 * [ 2 - 2*cos theta ] = 2*a^2 * \(1 - cos theta\)) Tj
T*
(   = 4*a^2 * sin^2\(theta / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   Therefore: [ \(x'\)^2 + \(y'\)^2 ]^\(3/2\) = [ 4*a^2 * sin^2\(theta / 2\) ]^\(3/2\) = 8*a^3 * sin^3\(theta) Tj
T*
(   / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Compute \(x' * y'' - y' * x''\):) Tj
T*
(   x' * y'' = a*\(1 - cos theta\) * a*cos theta = a^2 * \(cos theta - cos^2 theta\).) Tj
T*
(   y' * x'' = a*sin theta * a*sin theta = a^2 * sin^2 theta.) Tj
T*
(   x' * y'' - y' * x'' = a^2 * [ cos theta - \(cos^2 theta + sin^2 theta\) ] = a^2 * \(cos theta - 1\)) Tj
T*
(   = - a^2 * \(1 - cos theta\) = - 2*a^2 * sin^2\(theta / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   Magnitude = 2*a^2 * sin^2\(theta / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Calculate rho:) Tj
T*
(   rho = [ 8*a^3 * sin^3\(theta / 2\) ] / [ 2*a^2 * sin^2\(theta / 2\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = 4a * sin\(theta / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   For the cycloid, rho = 4a * sin\(theta / 2\) = 2 * sqrt\(2 * a * y\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
