BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the polar coordinate formula for radius of curvature: rho = \(r^2 + r'^2\)^\(3/2\) / |r^2 + 2*r'^2 - r * r''|. Find rho for the cardioid r = a*\(1 + cos theta\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Polar Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Parametric representation in polar coordinates: x = r * cos theta, y = r * sin theta, where r) Tj
T*
(   = r\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Derivatives with respect to theta \(denoted by primes\):) Tj
T*
(   x' = r' * cos theta - r * sin theta) Tj
T*
(   y' = r' * sin theta + r * cos theta.) Tj
T*
(   - Sum of squares:) Tj
T*
(   \(x'\)^2 + \(y'\)^2 = \(r' cos theta - r sin theta\)^2 + \(r' sin theta + r cos theta\)^2) Tj
T*
(   = \(r'\)^2 * \(cos^2 theta + sin^2 theta\) + r^2 * \(sin^2 theta + cos^2 theta\)) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
