(>> Solution to Question 16:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the pedal formula for the radius of curvature: rho = r * \(dr / dp\). Apply this formula to find the radius of curvature of the equiangular spiral r = a * e^\(theta * cot alpha\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Pedal Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - In polar coordinates, let P\(r, theta\) be a point on a curve, O be the pole, and p be the) Tj
T*
(   length of the perpendicular from the pole O to the tangent at P.) Tj
T*
(   - Let phi be the angle between the radius vector OP and the tangent at P:) Tj
T*
(   p = r * sin\(phi\).) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiate with respect to r:) Tj
T*
(   dp / dr = sin\(phi\) + r * cos\(phi\) * \(dphi / dr\).) Tj
T*
(   - We know from polar differential geometry:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(phi\) = r * \(dtheta / dr\) => sin\(phi\) = r * \(dtheta / ds\), cos\(phi\) = dr / ds.) Tj
T*
(   - Also, psi = theta + phi => dpsi / ds = dtheta / ds + dphi / ds.) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply dp/dr by dr/ds:) Tj
T*
(   \(dp / dr\) * \(dr / ds\) = [ sin\(phi\) + r * cos\(phi\) * \(dphi / dr\) ] * \(dr / ds\)) Tj
T*
(   dp / ds = sin\(phi\) * \(dr / ds\) + r * cos\(phi\) * \(dphi / ds\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute standard relations:) Tj
T*
(   dp / ds = r * \(dtheta / ds\) * \(dr / ds\) + r * \(dr / ds\) * \(dphi / ds\)) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
