(   = r * \(dr / ds\) * [ dtheta / ds + dphi / ds ]) Tj
T*
(   = r * \(dr / ds\) * \(dpsi / ds\)) Tj
T*
(   = \(r / rho\) * \(dr / ds\).) Tj
T*
(   Divide both sides by dr / ds:) Tj
T*
(   dp / dr = r / rho => rho = r * \(dr / dp\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Application to Equiangular Spiral:) Tj
T*
(   r = a * e^\(theta * cot alpha\).) Tj
T*
(   - Take natural logarithm: ln r = ln a + theta * cot alpha.) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiate with respect to theta:) Tj
T*
(   \(1 / r\) * \(dr / dtheta\) = cot alpha => dr / dtheta = r * cot alpha.) Tj
T*
(   - Relate to angle phi:) Tj
T*
(   tan\(phi\) = r * \(dtheta / dr\) = r / \(r * cot alpha\) = tan alpha => phi = alpha \(constant\).) Tj
T*
(   - Pedal equation:) Tj
T*
(   p = r * sin\(phi\) = r * sin\(alpha\).) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiate p with respect to r:) Tj
T*
(   dp / dr = sin\(alpha\) => dr / dp = 1 / sin\(alpha\) = csc\(alpha\).) Tj
T*
(   - Radius of Curvature:) Tj
T*
(   rho = r * \(dr / dp\) = r * csc\(alpha\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   The radius of curvature of the equiangular spiral is directly proportional to its distance r) Tj
T*
(   from the pole: rho = r * csc\(alpha\).) Tj
T*
