/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the coordinates \(x_bar, y_bar\) of the center of curvature for a curve y = f\(x\). Hence, find the equation of the circle of curvature at any point.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Derivation of Coordinates of Center of Curvature:) Tj
T*
(   - Let P\(x, y\) be a point on curve y = f\(x\). Let C\(x_bar, y_bar\) be the center of curvature at) Tj
T*
(   P.) Tj
T*
(   - The radius of curvature is rho, and C lies at distance rho along the inward normal to the) Tj
T*
(   curve at P.) Tj
T*
(   - Let psi be the inclination of the tangent at P to the x-axis: tan\(psi\) = y1 = dy/dx.) Tj
T*
(   - The inward normal makes an angle \(psi + pi/2\) with the x-axis:) Tj
T*
(   x_bar = x + rho * cos\(psi + pi/2\) = x - rho * sin\(psi\).) Tj
T*
(   y_bar = y + rho * sin\(psi + pi/2\) = y + rho * cos\(psi\).) Tj
T*
(   - From tan\(psi\) = y1:) Tj
T*
(   sin\(psi\) = y1 / sqrt\(1 + y1^2\), cos\(psi\) = 1 / sqrt\(1 + y1^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute rho = [ 1 + y1^2 ]^\(3/2\) / y2:) Tj
T*
(   x_bar = x - [ [ 1 + y1^2 ]^\(3/2\) / y2 ] * [ y1 / sqrt\(1 + y1^2\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = x - [ y1 * \(1 + y1^2\) ] / y2.) Tj
T*
(   y_bar = y + [ [ 1 + y1^2 ]^\(3/2\) / y2 ] * [ 1 / sqrt\(1 + y1^2\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = y + \(1 + y1^2\) / y2.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, the center of curvature is:) Tj
T*
(   x_bar = x - y1 * \(1 + y1^2\) / y2) Tj
T*
(   y_bar = y + \(1 + y1^2\) / y2. \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Equation of the Circle of Curvature:) Tj
T*
(   - The circle of curvature \(osculating circle\) at point P has center C\(x_bar, y_bar\) and radius) Tj
T*
(   R = rho.) Tj
T*
(   - Its Cartesian equation is:) Tj
T*
(   \(X - x_bar\)^2 + \(Y - y_bar\)^2 = rho^2,) Tj
T*
(   where \(X, Y\) are running coordinates on the circle.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
