/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Define the evolute of a curve. Derive the parametric coordinates of the center of curvature for the parabola y^2 = 4ax at point \(at^2, 2at\), and eliminate t to find the Cartesian equation of its evolute.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition:) Tj
T*
(   - The Evolute of a curve is the locus of all its centers of curvature.) Tj
T*
(   - Equivalently, it is the envelope of the family of normals to the curve.) Tj
T*
(   2. Derivatives at Parametric Point \(x = at^2, y = 2at\):) Tj
T*
(   - dx / dt = 2at, dy / dt = 2a.) Tj
T*
(   - y1 = dy / dx = \(2a\) / \(2at\) = 1 / t.) Tj
T*
(   - y2 = d/dx [ 1 / t ] = \(d/dt [ 1 / t ]\) / \(dx / dt\) = \(-1 / t^2\) / \(2at\) = -1 / \(2a * t^3\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Compute Center of Curvature \(x_bar, y_bar\):) Tj
T*
(   - 1 + y1^2 = 1 + 1/t^2 = \(t^2 + 1\) / t^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute x_bar:) Tj
T*
(   x_bar = x - y1 * \(1 + y1^2\) / y2) Tj
T*
(   = a*t^2 - \(1/t\) * [ \(t^2 + 1\) / t^2 ] / [ -1 / \(2a*t^3\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = a*t^2 + \(1/t\) * [ \(t^2 + 1\) / t^2 ] * \(2a*t^3\)) Tj
T*
(   = a*t^2 + 2a * \(t^2 + 1\) = a*t^2 + 2a*t^2 + 2a) Tj
T*
(   = 2a + 3a*t^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute y_bar:) Tj
T*
(   y_bar = y + \(1 + y1^2\) / y2) Tj
T*
(   = 2at + [ \(t^2 + 1\) / t^2 ] / [ -1 / \(2a*t^3\) ]) Tj
T*
(   = 2at - 2a*t^3 * [ \(t^2 + 1\) / t^2 ]) Tj
T*
(   = 2at - 2at * \(t^2 + 1\) = 2at - 2at^3 - 2at) Tj
T*
(   = -2a * t^3.) Tj
T*
(   4. Eliminate Parameter t to Obtain the Evolute:) Tj
T*
(   - From x_bar = 2a + 3a*t^2:) Tj
T*
(   3a * t^2 = x_bar - 2a => t^2 = \(x_bar - 2a\) / \(3a\).) Tj
T*
(   Raise to power 3: t^6 = \(x_bar - 2a\)^3 / \(27 * a^3\).) Tj
T*
(   - From y_bar = -2a * t^3:) Tj
T*
(   t^3 = - y_bar / \(2a\).) Tj
T*
(   Square both sides: t^6 = \(y_bar\)^2 / \(4 * a^2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Equate the two expressions for t^6:) Tj
T*
(   \(y_bar\)^2 / \(4 * a^2\) = \(x_bar - 2a\)^3 / \(27 * a^3\).) Tj
T*
(   - Multiply by 108 * a^3:) Tj
T*
(   27 * a * \(y_bar\)^2 = 4 * \(x_bar - 2a\)^3.) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion:) Tj
T*
(   Replacing \(x_bar, y_bar\) with running coordinates \(x, y\), the evolute of the parabola y^2 = 4ax) Tj
T*
(   is the semicubical parabola:) Tj
T*
(   27 a * y^2 = 4 * \(x - 2a\)^3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
