(   [Problem Statement]: Define an asymptote of an algebraic curve. Explain the systematic method for finding asymptotes parallel to coordinate axes and oblique asymptotes y = mx + c.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formal Definition:) Tj
T*
(   - A straight line L is said to be an asymptote of an infinite branch of a curve C if the) Tj
T*
(   perpendicular distance delta\(P, L\) from a point P on the curve to the line L tends to zero as P) Tj
T*
(   recedes to infinity along that branch:) Tj
T*
(   lim_{P -> infinity} delta\(P, L\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   2. Asymptotes Parallel to Coordinate Axes:) Tj
T*
(   Let the equation of the curve be f\(x, y\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Asymptotes parallel to y-axis \(Vertical Asymptotes\):) Tj
T*
