(   Arrange f\(x, y\) in descending powers of y:) Tj
T*
(   y^n * phi_0\(x\) + y^\(n-1\) * phi_1\(x\) + ... = 0.) Tj
T*
(   The asymptotes parallel to the y-axis are obtained by equating to zero the coefficient of the) Tj
T*
(   highest power of y:) Tj
T*
(   phi_0\(x\) = 0 \(provided phi_0\(x\) is not a mere numerical constant\).) Tj
T*
(   - Asymptotes parallel to x-axis \(Horizontal Asymptotes\):) Tj
T*
(   Arrange f\(x, y\) in descending powers of x:) Tj
T*
(   x^n * psi_0\(y\) + x^\(n-1\) * psi_1\(y\) + ... = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Equate to zero the coefficient of the highest power of x:) Tj
T*
(   psi_0\(y\) = 0 \(provided psi_0\(y\) is not constant\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Oblique Asymptotes \(y = mx + c\):) Tj
T*
(   - For an algebraic curve of degree n:) Tj
T*
(   f\(x, y\) = x^n * phi_n\(y/x\) + x^\(n-1\) * phi_{n-1}\(y/x\) + x^\(n-2\) * phi_{n-2}\(y/x\) + ... = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Put x = 1 and y = m in the terms of degree n:) Tj
T*
(   phi_n\(m\) = 0 gives the slopes m of the asymptotes.) Tj
T*
(   - For each non-repeated root m:) Tj
T*
(   c = - phi_{n-1}\(m\) / phi'_n\(m\) \(provided phi'_n\(m\) != 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - If m is a double root \(phi_n\(m\) = 0 and phi'_n\(m\) = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   \(c^2 / 2!\) * phi''_n\(m\) + c * phi'_{n-1}\(m\) + phi_{n-2}\(m\) = 0 gives two parallel asymptotes.) Tj
T*
