(>> Solution to Question 20:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Find all the asymptotes \(parallel and oblique\) of the cubic curve: x^3 + 3x^2*y - 4y^3 - x + y + 3 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Check for asymptotes parallel to axes:) Tj
T*
(   - Highest power of x is x^3; its coefficient is 1 \(constant\). No asymptote parallel to x-axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Highest power of y is y^3; its coefficient is -4 \(constant\). No asymptote parallel to y-axis.) Tj
T*
(   - Hence, all asymptotes are oblique.) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Collect terms of degree 3 \(highest degree n = 3\):) Tj
T*
(   Terms of degree 3: x^3 + 3*x^2*y - 4*y^3.) Tj
T*
(   Put x = 1, y = m to get phi_3\(m\):) Tj
T*
(   phi_3\(m\) = 1 + 3m - 4m^3.) Tj
T*
(   Set phi_3\(m\) = 0:) Tj
T*
(   4m^3 - 3m - 1 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Notice m = 1 is a root: 4\(1\) - 3\(1\) - 1 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Factor out \(m - 1\):) Tj
T*
(   \(m - 1\) * \(4m^2 + 4m + 1\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   => \(m - 1\) * \(2m + 1\)^2 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Roots: m1 = 1 \(single root\), m2 = m3 = -1/2 \(double root\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Collect terms of degree 2:) Tj
T*
(   There are NO degree 2 terms in the equation.) Tj
T*
(   phi_2\(m\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Collect terms of degree 1:) Tj
T*
(   Terms of degree 1: -x + y.) Tj
T*
(   phi_1\(m\) = -1 + m.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Compute c for single root m = 1:) Tj
T*
(   phi'_3\(m\) = d/dm [1 + 3m - 4m^3] = 3 - 12m^2.) Tj
T*
(   phi'_3\(1\) = 3 - 12 = -9.) Tj
T*
(   c = - phi_2\(1\) / phi'_3\(1\) = - 0 / \(-9\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Asymptote 1: y = 1*x + 0 => y - x = 0 \(or x - y = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 6: Compute c for double root m = -1/2:) Tj
T*
(   Since m = -1/2 is repeated, use the quadratic equation for c:) Tj
T*
(   \(c^2 / 2!\) * phi''_3\(m\) + c * phi'_2\(m\) + phi_1\(m\) = 0.) Tj
T*
ET

