(>> Solution to Question 23:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the systematic 6-step algorithm for tracing Cartesian curves: \(1\) Symmetry, \(2\) Origin and tangents, \(3\) Intercepts, \(4\) Asymptotes, \(5\) Regions of existence, \(6\) Sign of derivatives.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Systematic Curve Tracing Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   1. Symmetry:) Tj
T*
(   - About x-axis: If f\(x, -y\) = f\(x, y\) \(only even powers of y\).) Tj
T*
(   - About y-axis: If f\(-x, y\) = f\(x, y\) \(only even powers of x\).) Tj
T*
(   - About origin: If f\(-x, -y\) = f\(x, y\) \(opposite quadrants symmetric\).) Tj
T*
(   - About line y = x: If f\(y, x\) = f\(x, y\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Origin and Tangents at Origin:) Tj
T*
(   - Does the curve pass through \(0, 0\)? \(True if no constant term\).) Tj
T*
(   - If it passes through origin, find tangents by equating the lowest degree terms to zero.) Tj
T*
(   - Determine nature of origin \(smooth point, node, cusp, or isolated point\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Intercepts with Coordinate Axes:) Tj
T*
(   - x-intercepts: Set y = 0 and solve for x.) Tj
T*
ET

