T*
(   4. Asymptotes:) Tj
T*
(   - Vertical asymptotes: Equate coefficient of highest power of y to zero.) Tj
T*
(   - Horizontal asymptotes: Equate coefficient of highest power of x to zero.) Tj
T*
(   - Oblique asymptotes: Use y = mx + c with phi_n\(m\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   5. Region of Existence:) Tj
T*
(   - Solve explicitly for y in terms of x: y = +- g\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   - Determine intervals of x where g\(x\) is real \(i.e., radicands >= 0\).) Tj
T*
(   - If g\(x\) becomes imaginary, no part of the curve exists in that region.) Tj
T*
(   6. Special Points and Sign of Derivatives:) Tj
T*
(   - Compute dy/dx:) Tj
T*
(   * dy/dx = 0 gives points where tangents are parallel to x-axis \(extrema\).) Tj
T*
(   * dy/dx -> infinity gives points where tangents are vertical.) Tj
T*
(   - Compute d^2y/dx^2 for concavity and points of inflection.) Tj
