12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Trace the polar curve: Cardioid r = a * \(1 + cos theta\) \(where a > 0\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Step 1: Symmetry:) Tj
T*
(   Replacing theta with -theta leaves cos\(-theta\) = cos\(theta\) unchanged.) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, the cardioid is SYMMETRIC about the initial line \(polar axis theta = 0\).) Tj
T*
(   Step 2: Pole \(Origin\):) Tj
T*
(   Set r = 0: a * \(1 + cos theta\) = 0 => cos theta = -1 => theta = pi.) Tj
T*
(   The curve passes through the pole, and the tangent at the pole is theta = pi.) Tj
T*
(   Step 3: Range of r:) Tj
T*
(   Since -1 <= cos theta <= 1:) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum r occurs at theta = 0: r_max = a*\(1 + 1\) = 2a.) Tj
T*
(   - Minimum r occurs at theta = pi: r_min = a*\(1 - 1\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   For all theta, 0 <= r <= 2a; the curve is bounded within a circle of radius 2a.) Tj
T*
(   Step 4: Table of Values:) Tj
T*
(   theta = 0: r = 2a) Tj
T*
(   theta = pi/3: r = a*\(1 + 0.5\) = 1.5a) Tj
T*
(   theta = pi/2: r = a*\(1 + 0\) = a) Tj
T*
(   theta = 2pi/3: r = a*\(1 - 0.5\) = 0.5a) Tj
T*
(   theta = pi: r = 0.) Tj
T*
(   Step 5: Angle between Radius Vector and Tangent \(phi\):) Tj
T*
