(>> Solution to Question 27:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate the First and Second Derivative Tests for local extrema and points of inflection of a twice-differentiable function f\(x\). Prove the Second Derivative Test.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Formulations:) Tj
T*
(   - Critical Point: A point c in domain\(f\) where f'\(c\) = 0 \(stationary point\) or f'\(c\) does not) Tj
T*
(   exist.) Tj
T*
(   - First Derivative Test:) Tj
T*
(   * If f'\(x\) changes sign from positive to negative as x increases through c: Local Maximum.) Tj
T*
(   * If f'\(x\) changes sign from negative to positive as x increases through c: Local Minimum.) Tj
T*
(   * If f'\(x\) does not change sign: Neither \(Point of Inflection / Saddle\).) Tj
T*
(   - Second Derivative Test:) Tj
T*
(   Let f'\(c\) = 0 and f''\(c\) exist:) Tj
T*
(   * If f''\(c\) < 0: f has a Local Maximum at c.) Tj
T*
(   * If f''\(c\) > 0: f has a Local Minimum at c.) Tj
T*
(   * If f''\(c\) = 0: Test is inconclusive.) Tj
T*
(   - Point of Inflection: A point where the concavity changes \(f''\(x\) changes sign\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Proof of Second Derivative Test:) Tj
T*
(   - Case \(a\): Suppose f'\(c\) = 0 and f''\(c\) > 0.) Tj
T*
(   By definition of second derivative:) Tj
T*
(   f''\(c\) = lim_{h -> 0} [ f'\(c + h\) - f'\(c\) ] / h = lim_{h -> 0} [ f'\(c + h\) / h ] > 0.) Tj
T*
(   By the sign preservation theorem for limits, there exists delta > 0 such that for 0 < |h| <) Tj
T*
(   delta:) Tj
T*
(   f'\(c + h\) / h > 0.) Tj
T*
(   * For -delta < h < 0 \(left of c\): h < 0 implies f'\(c + h\) < 0 \(f is strictly decreasing\).) Tj
T*
(   * For 0 < h < delta \(right of c\): h > 0 implies f'\(c + h\) > 0 \(f is strictly increasing\).) Tj
T*
(   Thus, f'\(x\) changes from negative to positive as x passes through c.) Tj
T*
(   By the First Derivative Test, f attains a strict LOCAL MINIMUM at c.) Tj
T*
(   - Case \(b\): Suppose f'\(c\) = 0 and f''\(c\) < 0.) Tj
T*
(   f'\(c + h\) / h < 0 for all 0 < |h| < delta.) Tj
T*
(   * For h < 0: f'\(c + h\) > 0 \(strictly increasing\).) Tj
T*
(   * For h > 0: f'\(c + h\) < 0 \(strictly decreasing\).) Tj
T*
(   f'\(x\) changes from positive to negative.) Tj
T*
(   Hence, f attains a strict LOCAL MAXIMUM at c. \(Hence proved\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
