(   E + S <=k1 / k-1=> ES --k2--> E + P,) Tj
T*
(   where E = Free Enzyme, S = Substrate, ES = Enzyme-Substrate Complex, P = Product.) Tj
T*
(   2. Differential Rate Equations:) Tj
T*
(   - d[S] / dt = -k1 * [E] * [S] + k-1 * [ES].) Tj
T*
(   - d[ES] / dt = k1 * [E] * [S] - \(k-1 + k2\) * [ES].) Tj
T*
(   - d[P] / dt = k2 * [ES] = v \(reaction velocity\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Conservation of Total Enzyme:) Tj
T*
(   [E]t = [E] + [ES] => [E] = [E]t - [ES].) Tj
T*
(   4. Briggs-Haldane Quasi-Steady-State Assumption \(QSSA\):) Tj
T*
(   Because enzyme concentration is typically very small compared to substrate \([E]t << [S]\), the) Tj
T*
(   transient intermediate complex [ES] reaches a rapid balance where d[ES]/dt ~ 0:) Tj
T*
(   k1 * [E] * [S] - \(k-1 + k2\) * [ES] = 0.) Tj
T*
(   5. Solve for [ES]:) Tj
T*
(   Substitute [E] = [E]t - [ES]:) Tj
T*
(   k1 * \([E]t - [ES]\) * [S] = \(k-1 + k2\) * [ES]) Tj
T*
(   k1 * [E]t * [S] - k1 * [ES] * [S] = \(k-1 + k2\) * [ES]) Tj
T*
(   k1 * [E]t * [S] = [ k-1 + k2 + k1 * [S] ] * [ES].) Tj
T*
(   Divide numerator and denominator by k1:) Tj
T*
(   [ES] = [ [E]t * [S] ] / [ \(k-1 + k2\) / k1 + [S] ].) Tj
T*
(   6. Define Constants:) Tj
T*
(   - Michaelis constant: Km = \(k-1 + k2\) / k1.) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum velocity: Vmax = k2 * [E]t.) Tj
T*
(   7. Final Rate Equation:) Tj
T*
(   v = d[P] / dt = k2 * [ES] = [ k2 * [E]t * [S] ] / [ Km + [S] ]) Tj
T*
(   => v = \(Vmax * [S]\) / \(Km + [S]\). \(Proved\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
