(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Model microbial cell growth using the logistic differential equation dX/dt = r * X * \(1 - X / K\). Solve this non-linear ODE by separation of variables, find the inflection point, and determine when growth velocity is maximized.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Differential Equation Formulation:) Tj
T*
(   dX / dt = r * X * \(1 - X / K\),) Tj
T*
(   where X\(t\) is biomass concentration, r is intrinsic growth rate, and K is carrying capacity.) Tj
T*
(   2. Analytical Solution by Separation of Variables:) Tj
T*
(   dX / [ X * \(1 - X / K\) ] = r * dt) Tj
T*
(   => K * dX / [ X * \(K - X\) ] = r * dt.) Tj
T*
(   Partial fraction decomposition:) Tj
T*
(   [ 1/X + 1/\(K - X\) ] dX = r * dt.) Tj
T*
(   Integrate both sides:) Tj
T*
(   ln\(X\) - ln\(K - X\) = r * t + C) Tj
T*
(   ln [ X / \(K - X\) ] = r * t + C) Tj
T*
(   X / \(K - X\) = A * e^\(r*t\), where A = e^C.) Tj
T*
(   At t = 0, X\(0\) = X0:) Tj
T*
(   A = X0 / \(K - X0\).) Tj
T*
(   Solve for X\(t\):) Tj
T*
(   X = A * e^\(rt\) * \(K - X\) = A * K * e^\(rt\) - A * e^\(rt\) * X) Tj
T*
(   X * [ 1 + A * e^\(rt\) ] = K * A * e^\(rt\)) Tj
T*
(   X\(t\) = K / [ 1 + \(1/A\) * e^\(-rt\) ] = K / [ 1 + \(\(K - X0\) / X0\) * e^\(-rt\) ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Finding the Inflection Point \(Maximum Growth Rate\):) Tj
T*
(   - Growth velocity is: v\(X\) = dX / dt = r * X - \(r / K\) * X^2.) Tj
T*
(   - To maximize growth rate, differentiate v with respect to X:) Tj
T*
(   dv / dX = r - \(2r / K\) * X = 0) Tj
T*
(   => 2r * X / K = r => X = K / 2.) Tj
T*
ET

