(   - Second derivative: d^2v / dX^2 = -2r / K < 0 \(confirms global maximum\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thus, cell biomass growth rate is maximized precisely when biomass reaches HALF the carrying) Tj
T*
(   capacity: X = K / 2.) Tj
T*
(   - Maximum growth rate value:) Tj
T*
(   \(dX/dt\)_max = r * \(K / 2\) * \(1 - 1/2\) = r * K / 4.) Tj
T*
(   4. Time to Reach Inflection Point:) Tj
T*
(   Set X\(t_inf\) = K / 2:) Tj
T*
(   K / [ 1 + \(\(K - X0\) / X0\) * e^\(-r * t_inf\) ] = K / 2) Tj
T*
(   => 1 + \(\(K - X0\) / X0\) * e^\(-r * t_inf\) = 2) Tj
T*
(   => e^\(-r * t_inf\) = X0 / \(K - X0\) => t_inf = \(1 / r\) * ln\(\(K - X0\) / X0\).) Tj
