(>> Solution to Question 30:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze substrate inhibition enzyme kinetics governed by the Haldane model: v = Vmax * S / \(Km + S + S^2 / Ki\). Determine the optimal substrate concentration S_opt that maximizes reaction velocity and compute the maximum inhibited velocity v_opt.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Haldane Substrate Inhibition Model:) Tj
T*
(   - At high substrate concentrations, a second substrate molecule binds to the active site to) Tj
T*
(   form an inactive ternary complex ESS, reducing reaction velocity:) Tj
T*
(   v\(S\) = \(Vmax * S\) / \(Km + S + S^2 / Ki\),) Tj
T*
(   where Ki is the substrate inhibition constant.) Tj
T*
(   2. Differentiation to Find Extrema:) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiate v\(S\) with respect to S using the quotient rule:) Tj
T*
(   dv / dS = Vmax * [ \(Km + S + S^2 / Ki\) * 1 - S * \(1 + 2S / Ki\) ] / \(Km + S + S^2 / Ki\)^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Simplify numerator:) Tj
T*
(   Km + S + S^2 / Ki - S - 2*S^2 / Ki = Km - S^2 / Ki.) Tj
T*
(   - Set dv / dS = 0:) Tj
T*
(   Km - S^2 / Ki = 0 => S^2 / Ki = Km => S^2 = Km * Ki.) Tj
T*
(   - Since substrate concentration must be positive:) Tj
T*
(   S_opt = sqrt\(Km * Ki\). \(Geometric mean of Km and Ki\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Second Derivative Verification:) Tj
T*
(   - Evaluating d^2v / dS^2 at S_opt:) Tj
T*
(   Numerator derivative = -2*S / Ki < 0, while denominator is positive.) Tj
T*
(   Thus d^2v / dS^2 < 0 at S = S_opt, confirming that S_opt yields a unique global MAXIMUM) Tj
T*
(   velocity.) Tj
T*
(   4. Maximum Reaction Velocity v_opt:) Tj
T*
(   - Substitute S_opt = sqrt\(Km * Ki\) into v\(S\):) Tj
T*
(   v_opt = [ Vmax * sqrt\(Km * Ki\) ] / [ Km + sqrt\(Km * Ki\) + \(Km * Ki\) / Ki ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ Vmax * sqrt\(Km * Ki\) ] / [ Km + sqrt\(Km * Ki\) + Km ]) Tj
T*
(   = [ Vmax * sqrt\(Km * Ki\) ] / [ 2*Km + sqrt\(Km * Ki\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - Divide numerator and denominator by sqrt\(Km * Ki\):) Tj
T*
(   v_opt = Vmax / [ 1 + 2 * sqrt\(Km / Ki\) ].) Tj
T*
(   5. Biochemical Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - If Ki >> Km \(weak inhibition\): 2*sqrt\(Km/Ki\) << 1, and v_opt approaches Vmax.) Tj
T*
(   - If Ki is small \(strong inhibition\): v_opt is substantially lower than Vmax, and operating) Tj
T*
(   bioreactors above S_opt drastically reduces production throughput.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
